1. IT Project Management
Responsibilities:

Planning, executing, and closing IT projects
Managing project scope, schedule, and budget
Coordinating cross-functional teams
Identifying and mitigating risks
Communicating with stakeholders

Skills Required:

Strong organizational and leadership abilities
Knowledge of project management methodologies (Agile, Waterfall)
Technical understanding to communicate with development teams
Excellent communication and stakeholder management

Certifications:

Project Management Professional (PMP)
PRINCE2
Certified ScrumMaster (CSM)
ITIL certification can be helpful

Salary Range: $85,000-$130,000+ (varies by location and experience)
Growth Opportunities:

Senior Project Manager
Program Manager
IT Director
Portfolio Manager

2. Systems/Business Analyst
Responsibilities:

Gathering and analyzing business requirements
Translating business needs into technical specifications
Creating process flows and documentation
Testing and validating systems
Serving as a bridge between technical and non-technical stakeholders

Skills Required:

Strong analytical thinking
Requirements gathering techniques
Process mapping
Technical documentation
SQL knowledge often expected

Certifications:

Certified Business Analysis Professional (CBAP)
IIBA Entry Certificate in Business Analysis (ECBA)
Six Sigma certifications

Salary Range: $75,000-$110,000+
Growth Opportunities:

Senior Business Analyst
Solutions Architect
Product Owner
Business Systems Manager

3. DevOps Engineer
Responsibilities:

Automating infrastructure deployment
Implementing CI/CD pipelines
Managing cloud infrastructure
System monitoring and troubleshooting
Collaborating with development and operations teams

Skills Required:

Linux/Windows server administration
Scripting (Python, Bash, PowerShell)
Container technologies (Docker, Kubernetes)
Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, Ansible)
Cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP)

Certifications:

AWS/Azure/GCP cloud certifications
Docker Certified Associate
Kubernetes certifications (CKA, CKAD)
Red Hat Certified Engineer (RHCE)

Salary Range: $95,000-$140,000+
Growth Opportunities:

Senior DevOps Engineer
Site Reliability Engineer (SRE)
Cloud Architect
Infrastructure Architect

4. Information Security Specialist
Responsibilities:

Implementing security controls and policies
Monitoring systems for security breaches
Conducting vulnerability assessments
Responding to security incidents
Training staff on security best practices

Skills Required:

Network security knowledge
Security frameworks and compliance (NIST, ISO, etc.)
Risk assessment
Security tools and technologies

Certifications:

CompTIA Security+
Certified Information Systems Security Professional (CISSP)
Certified Ethical Hacker (CEH)
Certified Information Security Manager (CISM)

Salary Range: $90,000-$130,000+
Growth Opportunities:

Security Architect
Security Engineer
Chief Information Security Officer (CISO)
Security Consultant

5. Technical Product Manager
Responsibilities:

Defining product vision and strategy
Creating and prioritizing product backlog
Working with development teams to deliver features
Gathering customer feedback and market research
Making data-driven product decisions

Skills Required:

Technical understanding to work with engineers
Product lifecycle management
User experience concepts
Market analysis
Communication and presentation skills

Certifications:

Certified Scrum Product Owner (CSPO)
Professional Scrum Product Owner (PSPO)
Product Management certifications from Product School

Salary Range: $90,000-$140,000+
Growth Opportunities:

Senior Product Manager
Director of Product
VP of Product
Chief Product Officer

